            "label": {
              "en": "equation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "(x-3)² + (y+2)² = 25"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Ellipses and hyperbolas</h3>An ellipse: \\( \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1 \\). A hyperbola: \\( \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1 \\). EST II may ask you to identify the type of conic from a standard-form equation and state key features like vertices, foci, or asymptotes.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Circles & Coordinate Geometry",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Circle equation: \\((x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2\\). A tangent to a circle at point \\(P\\) is perpendicular to the radius at \\(P\\). Circle theorems: angle at centre = twice angle at circumference; angles in same segment are equal; tangent-radius angle = 90°. Chord perpendicular bisector passes through the centre.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Tangent from external point",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A circle has centre \\(O(3,2)\\) and radius 5. Point \\(P(10,2)\\) lies outside the circle. Find the length of the tangent from \\(P\\) to the circle. <p>\\(OP = \\sqrt{(10-3)^2+(2-2)^2} = 7\\). Tangent length \\(= \\sqrt{OP^2 - r^2} = \\sqrt{49-25} = \\sqrt{24} = 2\\sqrt{6}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the equation of the circle that passes through \\((0,0)\\), \\((6,0)\\) and \\((0,8)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Let \\((x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2\\). Using \\((0,0)\\): \\(h^2+k^2=r^2\\). Using \\((6,0)\\): \\((6-h)^2+k^2=r^2\\) gives \\(h=3\\). Using \\((0,8)\\): \\(h^2+(8-k)^2=r^2\\) gives \\(k=4\\). So \\(r^2=25\\). Equation: \\((x-3)^2+(y-4)^2=25\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
